        "textContent": {
          "paragraph-359ff3b9-bfa7-4205-86ee-a1566af90d46": "Rect 125",
          "paragraph-35082f6d-787a-4332-9a4d-52512e3e7ec3": "A square poster asks for a steadier balance between display and text. The large numeral anchors the field, while the body block keeps the reading pace measured and calm. Captions act as small positional notes, reinforcing the module structure without competing for attention. The grid does not decorate the page; it establishes a disciplined order that lets contrast, spacing, and silence work together as one composition.",
          "paragraph-8ddb833d-2dcb-40bc-bf4f-036325dcd3f2": "Poster study,\nsquare field,\n2026",
          "paragraph-0e70b6b7-cf3d-4cdd-82d1-bfac2d6f0f7e": "Baseline rhythm,\nmodule note,\n12 pt",
          "paragraph-1af6504c-87af-489f-a8bc-c77c21e29677": "Left column,\nimage field,\ncaption",
          "paragraph-e12fa407-4915-4842-9e1c-3d49642fc153": "Display block,\nlower edge,\naligned",
          "paragraph-443948fe-0b57-4359-8fb1-9e964c08e1c5": "Body column,\ntop anchor,\nmeasured",
          "paragraph-2c26f239-b2d4-48f0-a4b9-6caa9e90da70": "Monochrome palette,\nneutral paper\ntone",
          "paragraph-88aa199e-7f9d-4e67-86fa-4ff6bcc08b78": "Swiss Grid Generator\n<%date%>",
          "paragraph-5da9e934-ef3b-42bc-909d-9d83f864d757": "The side text explains how repetition and variation can share the same frame. Each paragraph holds roughly equal weight, yet the differing positions create a clear sequence across the poster. This is where Swiss practice becomes useful: not as style alone, but as a method for setting relation, interval, and emphasis before local detail is refined. The result is a page that feels exact, quiet, and still open enough for visual energy.",
          "paragraph-de31370f-bd9c-4bf6-9c9e-3c638649e3dc": "The lower text block carries the denser reading voice. It supports the headline without enlarging it and gives the poster a second register of information. Because every line still belongs to the same baseline system, the composition stays coherent even when the masses differ. What appears expressive on the surface is therefore grounded in measured decisions about rows, spans, offsets, and the controlled use of editorial contrast."
        },
